I am using this directory for equations of rank-0 fibrations on K3 surfaces
of rank 20, sorted by discriminant and restricted to the ones that are defined
over Q.  Each file defines the fibrations of a given discriminant in a
variable ecs_disc*.  The twists that are rational 202 surfaces can be found
using the function twists in good_twists.mag.  Standard Magma functions
can be used for the L-polynomials, but I have not collected these.  I have
made no attempt to find modular forms for most of them.

Many of these are already in Schutt's paper, but some of them are found
in other ways: when the torsion is trivial one can try to specialize
constructions in Elkies-Kumar, when it is not one can use normal forms
for elliptic curves with torsion, etc.

Note that there can be some tricky cases where there are two pairs of fibres
of the same type and one has to choose which pair is defined over Q.
This may happen at level 36 with I8^* I4I4I3I3, for example.